 write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{3}+9y\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{3}+9y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =9{y}^{2}+9 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-73064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5b8f4cf28e9550c1fde85ca097e20a22a5174783e35800683a70e197fa88eed"} {"question" "q-73064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-73064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{{({f}^{-1}(x))}^{2}+1}"] [