\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5b8f4cf28e9550c1fde85ca097e20a22a5174783e35800683a70e197fa88eed"} {"question" "q-110045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}+16({h}^{-1}(x))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{10({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}+3({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-8({h}^{-1}(x))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-6({h}^{-1}(x))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-2({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{20({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+6({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}-16({h}^{-1}(x))}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $h(x)=8{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-12,$ find ${({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${h}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y=8{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-12,$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=8{y}^{6}+4{y}^{4}+3{y}^{3}-12\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={h}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(8{y}^{6}+4{y}^{4}+3{y}^{3}-12) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =48{y}^{5}+16{y}^{3}+9{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{48{y}^{5}+16{y}^{3}+9{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${h}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={h}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{h}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}} \\\\ {({h}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b5b8f4cf28e9550c1fde85ca097e20a22a5174783e35800683a70e197fa88eed"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{24({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-8({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{4}-16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}-3({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+8({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{48({h}^{-1}(x))^{5}+16({h}^{-1}(x))^{3}+9({h}^{-1}(x))^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x)={sin}^{4}⁡({x}^{3}),$ find ${({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x)$ as a function of ${f}^{-1}(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Step 1:** First, we write the inverse function implicitly. The given function is $y={sin}^{4}⁡({x}^{3}),$ and to write the inverse function implicitly, we swap $x$ and $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\nx={sin}^{4}⁡({y}^{3})\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({sin}^{4}⁡({y}^{3})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =4{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =12{y}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{12{y}^{2}{sin}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{3})} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({y}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({y}^{3})}{12{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${f}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{f}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}} \\\\ {({f}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})\\operatorname{sec}⁡({[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{3})}{12{[{f}^{-1}(x)]}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040095/state.json" "file_sha256" "a52e91968bb249d67ea869beeb52d161a3c13d1f610c18a436cfd4e6b842442b"} {"question" "q-110048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "cat